      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. They reported that since the taxonomy change on 2026-02-20, Event Nexus search results returned many low-relevance hits and duplicates, increasing manual triage time to about 6 hours per day. The root cause was identified as the Event Nexus index weighting still referencing old schema fields, with schema registry versions diverging from the Event Nexus mappings, causing poor search relevance and duplicate results [art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194].\n\nThe proof plan proposed to get BlueHarbor comfortable with renewal included:\n\n- Updating the index weighting and adding a translation/mapping layer that maps new taxonomy terms to historical query tokens for the top 20 saved searches.\n\n- Timeline and steps:\n  1) Receive schema registry export and 14 days of anonymized query logs from BlueHarbor by 2026-03-19.\n  2) Start an A/B test in staging on 2026-03-22, lasting 5 business days for tuning plus 2 business days for validation (7-10 business days total).\n  3) Validation criteria: top-5 correct hit rate \u2265 80% for prioritized queries; no regression in EN-RULES-ENGINE suppression logic; incident correlation latency under 200ms.\n  4) If validation passes, perform a 1-day production rollout with 72 hours monitoring.\n\n- Professional services offer: a 90-day fixed-price engagement at $48k to implement tuning, build the mapping layer, and run the proof, with a 30% discount if BlueHarbor commits to Orchestrator seat expansion concurrently.\n\n- A conditional credit clause was proposed: if the proof does not meet the agreed top-5 accuracy uplift within 10 business days, BlueHarbor would receive a one-quarter invoice credit prorated against the renewal for the upcoming year.\n\n- Risks and mitigations included fallback to a full reindex (~15 TB, 48 hours compute, ~$25k cost) if mapping is insufficient, and discouragement of parallel use of NoiseGuard deduplication tool during the proof.\n\n- Action items included drafting the SOW addendum with the conditional credit clause by 2026-03-19 and provisioning staging snapshots [art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194].\n\nThus, BlueHarbor Logistics is the customer with the issue starting after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout, and the detailed proof plan with timeline, validation criteria, professional services offer, conditional credit, and fallback reindex was proposed to secure their renewal comfort.",
