      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were the \"department\" and \"businessUnit\" attributes. These were used inconsistently across teams: Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant, while Payments Ops used department=payments. This inconsistency caused ingestion normalization failures and routing mismatches in the Rules Engine, leading to role provisioning delays and failures [art_79f625aafa16].\n\nJin proposed a fast fix to add a preprocessing mapping rule in Signal Ingest that maps one attribute to the other (for example, businessUnit -> department) to produce a normalized canonical field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only, hot-reloadable change that does not require Okta change control or appliance restarts, enabling immediate remediation without waiting 2-4 weeks for Okta changes [art_79f625aafa16], [art_e60697c15fce].",
      "source_ids": [
