      "answer": "There is a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple accounts, not just MapleBridge. The customers sharing this failure pattern are:\n\n- MapleBridge Insurance\n- MapleFork Franchise Systems\n- MapleWest Bank\n- MapleBay Marketplace\n- MapleRegional Transit Authority\n- MaplePath Career Institute\n- City of Verdant Bay\n\nThe shared failure pattern in plain English is that after migrating from legacy workflow tooling to the Orchestrator product, approval workflows for Canada-specific policies are failing due to incorrect rule evaluation precedence. Specifically, global default approval rules are overriding or bypassing region-specific (country or province) approval rules. This causes approval requests that should be routed to Canada-specific approvers to be either skipped, auto-denied, stuck in pending states, or routed incorrectly to global approvers. The root cause involves the order in which policy rules are evaluated, schema key mismatches (e.g., 'country_code' vs 'country'), and delayed synchronization of schema registry versions across evaluation clusters. This leads to automated approvals bypassing required Canada-specific gating, resulting in compliance risks and manual intervention needs.\n\nThis pattern has been observed in multiple tenants with similar symptoms: approvals stuck or auto-denied, missing audit entries, and escalations due to blocked or misrouted approvals. The issue started after migrations around February-March 2026 and affects various approval flows including payroll, procurement, and claims processing.\n\n[art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_3db205cb21ca, art_e697b3abe158]",
